{"audit_run_id":"audit:970888b153da4a689352ace6bddd02b9","completed_at":"2026-07-27T20:00:00Z","coverage_status":"covered","emitted_record_refs":[],"extensions":{"x-candidate-spans":[{"end_column":90,"end_line":3,"start_column":1,"start_line":3,"text":"The file `nestling_mass.csv` holds the day-12 measurements from the supplementary-feeding"},{"end_column":64,"end_line":4,"start_column":1,"start_line":4,"text":"experiment in the great tit (*Parus major*) nestbox population."},{"end_column":95,"end_line":8,"start_column":1,"start_line":8,"text":"One row is one nestling, weighed and measured once on day 12 after hatching. A row carries the"},{"end_column":98,"end_line":9,"start_column":1,"start_line":9,"text":"chick's own two measurements (mass and tarsus length) together with the nestbox it came from, the"},{"end_column":69,"end_line":10,"start_column":1,"start_line":10,"text":"feeding treatment that box received, and the date its brood hatched."},{"end_column":43,"end_line":14,"start_column":1,"start_line":14,"text":"- 16 nestboxes (broods) entered the study."},{"end_column":68,"end_line":15,"start_column":1,"start_line":15,"text":"- Each of those boxes held exactly 4 surviving nestlings on day 12."},{"end_column":60,"end_line":16,"start_column":1,"start_line":16,"text":"- The file therefore has 64 data rows, plus one header row."},{"end_column":59,"end_line":17,"start_column":1,"start_line":17,"text":"- Every chick appears once; there are no repeat weighings."},{"end_column":98,"end_line":18,"start_column":1,"start_line":18,"text":"- The four chicks in a box share the same `nest_tag`, `food_treatment`, and `hatch_date`, because"},{"end_column":92,"end_line":19,"start_column":3,"start_line":19,"text":"treatment was applied to whole broods at the box and the whole brood hatched on one date."},{"end_column":49,"end_line":20,"start_column":1,"start_line":20,"text":"- Hatch dates run from 2026-04-22 to 2026-05-06."},{"end_column":70,"end_line":21,"start_column":1,"start_line":21,"text":"- Ring numbers run from A1201 to A1264, in the order the rows appear."},{"end_column":93,"end_line":22,"start_column":1,"start_line":22,"text":"- Rows are ordered nest by nest, following the field notebook, and the nest tags are the box"},{"end_column":90,"end_line":23,"start_column":3,"start_line":23,"text":"numbers actually used in the plot, so the numbering has gaps (NB-01, NB-02, ... NB-23)."},{"end_column":51,"end_line":27,"start_column":1,"start_line":27,"text":"| Group | Meaning | Nestboxes | Nestlings (rows) |"},{"end_column":18,"end_line":28,"start_column":1,"start_line":28,"text":"|---|---|---|---|"},{"end_column":102,"end_line":29,"start_column":1,"start_line":29,"text":"| `supplemented` | A mealworm feeder was placed within 5 m of the box from hatching onward | 8 | 32 |"},{"end_column":68,"end_line":30,"start_column":1,"start_line":30,"text":"| `control` | No feeder; the box was left unsupplemented | 8 | 32 |"},{"end_column":32,"end_line":34,"start_column":1,"start_line":34,"text":"| Column | Type | Description |"},{"end_column":14,"end_line":35,"start_column":1,"start_line":35,"text":"|---|---|---|"},{"end_column":190,"end_line":36,"start_column":1,"start_line":36,"text":"| `nest_tag` | string | Identifier of the nestbox the chick came from, written as `NB-` plus a two-digit box number (for example `NB-04`). Sixteen distinct tags; four rows share each tag. |"},{"end_column":128,"end_line":37,"start_column":1,"start_line":37,"text":"| `food_treatment` | string | The feeding treatment the box received: `supplemented` or `control`. Constant within a nestbox. |"},{"end_column":150,"end_line":38,"start_column":1,"start_line":38,"text":"| `chick_ring` | string | The ring number of the individual nestling (for example `A1201`). Unique across the whole file, so it identifies the row. |"},{"end_column":101,"end_line":39,"start_column":1,"start_line":39,"text":"| `hatch_date` | date (ISO, `YYYY-MM-DD`) | The date the brood hatched. Constant within a nestbox. |"},{"end_column":140,"end_line":40,"start_column":1,"start_line":40,"text":"| `mass_g_day12` | number (grams, 1 decimal place) | Body mass of the nestling on day 12 after hatching. This is the outcome of interest. |"},{"end_column":144,"end_line":41,"start_column":1,"start_line":41,"text":"| `tarsus_mm` | number (millimetres, 1 decimal place) | Tarsus length of the same nestling on day 12, recorded as a measure of skeletal size. |"},{"end_column":85,"end_line":45,"start_column":1,"start_line":45,"text":"The file was produced by `make_data.py` in this directory, using a fixed random seed"},{"end_column":98,"end_line":46,"start_column":1,"start_line":46,"text":"(`SEED = 20260421`) so the values reproduce exactly. Re-running `python3 make_data.py` overwrites"},{"end_column":45,"end_line":47,"start_column":1,"start_line":47,"text":"`nestling_mass.csv` with the identical file."}],"x-expected-count-method-declarations":[],"x-explicit-directional-claims":[],"x-explicit-expected-count-sensitivities":[],"x-explicit-quantitative-claims":[]},"opaque_constructs":[],"parser_disagreement":null,"parser_id":"parser:markdown-inventory","parser_result_id":"parser-result:7110aeee682144d34686","parser_version":"0.2.0","provenance":{"actor":{"actor_id":"parser:markdown-inventory","actor_kind":"parser"},"created_at":"2026-07-27T20:00:00Z","method":"static_inventory","tool":"sc-referee","tool_version":"0.3.0"},"record_type":"parser_result","schema_version":"0.19.0","source_ref":{"content_digest":"sha256:cf4721bc124a3926e64112a9f195e6f720e1d7029419336caea5fe24f31c7bb5","end_line":47,"locator":"DATA_DESCRIPTION.md:1-47","path":"DATA_DESCRIPTION.md","source_kind":"file_span","start_line":1},"started_at":"2026-07-27T20:00:00Z","state":"parsed","syntax_issues":[]}
{"audit_run_id":"audit:970888b153da4a689352ace6bddd02b9","completed_at":"2026-07-27T20:00:00Z","coverage_status":"covered","emitted_record_refs":[],"extensions":{"x-candidate-spans":[{"end_column":98,"end_line":5,"start_column":1,"start_line":5,"text":"Compare `mass_g_day12` between the two levels of `food_treatment` (`supplemented` and `control`)."},{"end_column":103,"end_line":9,"start_column":1,"start_line":9,"text":"The independent experimental unit is the nestbox (brood). The column `nest_tag` carries the value that"},{"end_column":194,"end_line":10,"start_column":1,"start_line":10,"text":"identifies it: each nestbox (brood) has one distinct `nest_tag` value. The feeding treatment was applied to whole broods at the nestbox, so the nestbox is the unit that was assigned to a group."},{"end_column":101,"end_line":14,"start_column":1,"start_line":14,"text":"The analysis is a two-group comparison of `mass_g_day12` between the two levels of `food_treatment`."},{"end_column":89,"end_line":15,"start_column":1,"start_line":15,"text":"This protocol does not select, require, or exclude any particular statistical procedure."}],"x-expected-count-method-declarations":[],"x-explicit-directional-claims":[],"x-explicit-expected-count-sensitivities":[],"x-explicit-quantitative-claims":[]},"opaque_constructs":[],"parser_disagreement":null,"parser_id":"parser:markdown-inventory","parser_result_id":"parser-result:4734c26742b190e4f0de","parser_version":"0.2.0","provenance":{"actor":{"actor_id":"parser:markdown-inventory","actor_kind":"parser"},"created_at":"2026-07-27T20:00:00Z","method":"static_inventory","tool":"sc-referee","tool_version":"0.3.0"},"record_type":"parser_result","schema_version":"0.19.0","source_ref":{"content_digest":"sha256:40531b6c7ccc02e7073a43ddcd334e75116935a1fc8c161c54dc3bdc21866bcd","end_line":15,"locator":"PROTOCOL.md:1-15","path":"PROTOCOL.md","source_kind":"file_span","start_line":1},"started_at":"2026-07-27T20:00:00Z","state":"parsed","syntax_issues":[]}
